<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">stone-golem</ansi>

The Stone Golem is a formation anchor: slow, heavily plated and unmoved by
fear. It is a construct, so it is kept differently from any other companion
(<ansi fg="command">help creatures</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Stone Golem is</ansi>

  Health      12 to start, 1.5 a level (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 0.9 and Evasion 0.6 a level (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Attack      a stone fist, 2d5
  Stats       vitality 4, strength 3 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Gear        none: it wears nothing but its own stone
  Upkeep      needs no food, drink or rest, takes no bed at an inn, and
              never loses heart, so it never drifts or deserts
  Mends       only with stone mortar (<ansi fg="command">help repair</ansi>); rest, camp and the
              slow trickle between fights do nothing for it
  Carries     nothing

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks of the Stone Golem</ansi>

  Level 1   <ansi fg="yellow">Stone body</ansi>  +30 armor, but it acts 15% less often and spells
                       hit it 25% harder
  Level 1   <ansi fg="yellow">Anchor</ansi>      allies in its row take 10% less damage (auras do not
                       stack within a row; <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>)
  Level 10  <ansi fg="yellow">Granite</ansi>     its armor rises to +40 in all, and its fist lands
                       2 harder
  Level 20  <ansi fg="yellow">Bedrock</ansi>     its row takes 15% less damage in all, and its fist
                       lands 4 harder in all

It has no promotion and no talents. Healing spells still heal it, and a battle
cannot give it a lasting wound (stone cracks, and repair closes the crack).
Its default target rule is <ansi fg="command">nearest</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Getting a Stone Golem</ansi>

Cairn is hiring at the Waymark Inn in Dunmar for 180 gold
(<ansi fg="command">company recruit</ansi>). Buy stone mortar at the Dunmar market and keep a few
in your pack.
